WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.167
-Welcome, welcome, welcome.

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.334
Thank you so much.
-Thank you.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.667
-Thank you.
-This is your U.S. TV debut.

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:06.901
-Yes.
-It is.

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:08.834
-It is tonight.
I have to say, we tweeted out

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.267
that you guys were coming on.

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.100
And I want to say,
in maybe 5 seconds,

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.801
it was 20,000 likes, and we were
all trending at the same time.

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:17.968
So, you have
a lot of fans out there.

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:19.133
-Yeah.
-It's fun, it's fun.

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:20.834
-Yeah.
"Young Royals" is one of

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:22.734
the biggest shows in Sweden,

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:26.033
and now it's getting popular
all over the world.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:28.033
Here you are on the cover
of "Vogue Scandinavia."

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:29.434
-Whoo!
-Look at this.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:33.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:37.467
Omar, did you expect this show
to take off like this?

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:41.567
-I mean, we kind of
saw that coming, I would say.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:42.834
[ Laughter ]
But --

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:45.200
-Oh, please.
-But -- But -- But --

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.634
Let me finish.

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:49.834
Because I really
love the storyline.

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:54.767
And I fell in love with
the script when I first read it.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:57.300
And now --

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.868
The only thing, though --
I could never imagine

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:03.634
that we would be on
"The Fallon Show" in New York.

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:05.467
So now it's kind of, like,
getting to me.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:07.767
-Oh, yeah, all right.
Okay, that's good.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.467
-So, I'm like,
"Oh, it's pretty --

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:12.334
it's pretty big now, yeah."
-Slowly realizing.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:13.701
-Yeah.
-Slowly.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.901
-Edvin, can you tell everyone
what the show is about,

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:19.000
for people who haven't seen it?
-Yeah, Well, in short,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.133
it's a story about freedom
and being who you are.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:26.267
But we follow
the prince of Sweden.

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:29.033
And he's a bit
of a party prince, I guess.

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:30.033
-Yeah.
-Whoo!

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:32.400
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.033
Not that kind of party Prince.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:37.501
-He gets sent to this
boarding school in Sweden,

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:38.667
named Hillerska.

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:42.734
And he meets Simon,
and he falls in love.

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:44.300
That creates
all kinds of issues.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.100
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.434
It is so well done, by the way.

00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:50.033
I will also give props
to Netflix

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:53.133
because they do a dubbing,
audio dubbing,

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:55.234
in English perfectly,
by the way.

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:57.767
-But you know that's us.
-No.

00:01:57.767 --> 00:01:59.434
Doing the -- yeah.
-That's you doing the voice?

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:01.000
-Yeah, we're doing
the English dubbing.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.267
-I was gonna say, whoever does
the voice sounds just like you.

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:04.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:06.634
Wait. So you act --
you act the whole show --

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:09.501
You do it in...
-Swedish and in English, yeah.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:10.834
-Whoa!
-Yeah.

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:12.234
-You're putting the work in,
man.

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:14.534
Wow! That's fantastic.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.067
-Yeah.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:17.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:18.200
-You know how to do it.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.901
These guys are putting
the work in.

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:22.400
You're so,uh --
-I love this crowd.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.868
-Yeah. Well...
-They're amazing.

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:26.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You guys are...

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.367
-The energy.
-You feel the energy, right?

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:32.767
-Yeah, yeah.
-I know, yeah.

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:34.767
You have fans, by the way --

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:38.834
Obviously, you have a giant --
you were in a giant boy band.

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:40.734
-Giant boy band.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:43.601
-I would say giant.
-In Sweden, at least, yeah.

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.100
-Yeah, in Sweden, yeah.
But, I mean,

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.434
you opened for One Direction.
-Yeah.

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:48.534
-Here's a picture of you.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:53.100
-Look at that guy.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:56.200
Look at that cute little guy.
-Look at that.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.634
-Hi, Harry.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:01.467
-Hi, Harry. What do you remember
about this tour?

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:05.167
-Um, it was a crazy experience.

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:08.667
It was in one of
the biggest arenas in Sweden.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:11.934
And we were a band for a year

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:13.567
when we opened for
One Direction.

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:14.934
-Oh, my gosh.
-Yeah.

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:17.501
And we were like 15.
-Coming from playing, like,

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:19.968
high school, from a garage
or someone's living room

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:21.734
to an arena...
-Well, almost, yeah, yeah.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.400
-We did these, like, flash mobs
in the streets.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.667
-Yeah, our thing was performing
on the streets

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:29.701
and recording it, like,
lip-syncing to our songs.

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:32.300
And then we uploaded it
on YouTube.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.334
And then, we ended up there.

00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:36.400
-Yeah, I guess
that's a big deal.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.567
-That's crazy.
-As you do.

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:39.501
-Is this before the --
because Justin Bieber --

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:40.634
I remember
you opened for Bieber,

00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:41.934
and that was the big break.

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:45.400
-Yeah. Well, so, that was
our first gig as a group at all.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.901
So, the first time we ever
went up on stage together,

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:51.000
it was opening for Justin Bieber
three nights in a row.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.767
Hi, Justin!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:55.868
-Hi, Justin, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.400
When you first
auditioned together,

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.734
did you have instant chemistry
and go,

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:02.901
"Oh, I can work with this guy.
We're gonna be buddies."

00:04:02.901 --> 00:04:06.734
-Well, yeah, but the thing was,
Omar was a bit late.

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:07.968
-Ooh!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:10.234
-Yeah, you had missed a bus
or something.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:12.934
So, he came in, like,
all sweaty and stressed out.

00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:15.434
And the thing was,
I remember, I saw his face,

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:18.367
and I recognized him because
he was famous already.

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:20.100
He was a celebrity in Sweden
because of the band.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:24.501
But I also -- I attended that
Justin Bieber concert in 2013.

00:04:24.501 --> 00:04:26.267
-You were there?
-Yeah, I was there.

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:28.067
-You were like 10.
-Yeah, I was like

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.033
10 years old or something.
Yeah.

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:32.634
I just went with a buddy
'cause he had a ticket over.

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:35.501
And then, these guys opened.
They were singing a song

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:37.834
about kangaroos.
-Now forever you'll be --

00:04:37.834 --> 00:04:40.300
But now together you guys
will be always known as --

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.801
What are they calling you now?
Wilmon?

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:43.501
-Yeah, Wilmon.
-Yeah.

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:46.767
-Yeah, Wilmon.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:50.167
-I got to say, also,
when we booked you on the show,

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:51.634
everyone was going --
fans were going nuts.

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:54.801
And they're like, "Well, you
better bring back season three.

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:56.000
'Cause season one and two --

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.601
They better be coming back
for season three."

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.501
And I go,
"I have nothing to do with this.

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:01.801
I'm just a fan
of 'Young Royals.'"

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.400
I'm just saying
it's a good show

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.567
and everyone
should check it out.

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:06.067
It's done well.
It's acted well.

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.133
It's written well.
And then one fan

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:10.467
actually tweeted
every single day,

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:11.934
"Good morning, Netflix.

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:14.167
Another beautiful day
to renew 'Young Royals.'"

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:16.067
Every single day.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:18.167
Every single day.
Well, I'm happy to say,

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:20.234
it just got picked up
for season three.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:21.634
So, congratulations.
-Yay!

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:24.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.434 --> 00:05:26.167
What can we --

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:31.167
What can we say about season
three without spoiling anything?

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:33.133
-Well, I mean,
it's still very early.

00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:34.601
The script
is still being written.

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:38.434
But we know that it's going
to be the final season.

00:05:38.434 --> 00:05:40.501
So -- which is kind of --
It's bittersweet.

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:43.601
But we're looking forward
for this chapter to close

00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:44.934
and what's gonna happen
with Simon and Wilhelm.

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:47.133
-Yeah, and we're looking forward
to see them smile.

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:49.167
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:51.400
-They -- all right.
-They don't smile a lot.

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:52.968
-They might smile
in season three.

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:54.968
-Hopefully.
-I want to show everyone a clip

00:05:54.968 --> 00:05:56.834
here from season two
of "Young Royals."

00:05:56.834 --> 00:05:58.033
Take a look at this.

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:24.367
-Edvin Ryding, Omar Rudberg!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:26.567
Season one and two
of "Young Royals"

00:06:26.567 --> 00:06:28.634
are streaming now on Netflix.

